      "document_summary": "Review by Nicoletta Momigliano in Bryn Mawr Classical
Review (2009) of Cathy Gere’s book \"Knossos and the Prophets of Modernism\". 
The review outlines Gere’s exploration of how Arthur Evans and other figures 
constructed and interpreted Minoan civilization in the early 20th century, 
emphasizing modernist and prophetic modes of reception. Within this context, the
review notes that Evans and later interpreters sometimes read Mycenaean 
artefacts, including the so‑called \"Ring of Nestor\", as representations of the
Minoan soul or \"psyche\". This is used as an example of the imaginative, 
psychological, and spiritual readings imposed on Aegean Bronze Age artefacts in 
modernist discourse, rather than a detailed technical or archaeological analysis
of the ring itself.",
