Minoan gold signet ring dating to around 1500 BCE, with dimensions approximately
2.2 cm in height and 3.9 cm in length, and attributes its current location to 
the Ashmolean Museum in Oxford under inventory number AN1938.1130. The context 
presents the ring as a piece of Aegean glyptic art with elaborate imagery. The 
caption and associated text do not indicate any inscribed legend on the ring; it
is treated as a carved signet ring with figural decoration only.",
      "source_ref": "s9"
    }
